+| `worktree_bead_query_failed` | The one bulk bead read ran and did not answer. `reason`: `bead_query_timed_out` (slower than the seconds the run had left — the detail names them) or `bead_query_failed` (non-zero exit). The detail also names the TRANSPORT it used: `bd pinned to <rig root>` (the cheap read) or `gc bd --rig <rig>` (the wrapper) | Nothing was examined this cycle. **`bead_query_timed_out` on a small remaining budget is the reaper's clock, not the store** — compare the detail's "Ns left of the Ms budget" before suspecting the endpoint. **A timeout with most of the budget unspent is NOT automatically the endpoint either** — a single wrapped call has been measured at 5.4s on this city, which is most of an 8s budget on its own (gcp-uzq0). Before suspecting the store, time the transport the detail names against the rig's own endpoint: if the pinned read answers fast and only the wrapper is slow, the store is healthy and the cost is gc's. Chasing Dolt on this line has produced two wrong diagnoses already |
